## Tangible workflow execution framing

2026-06-09 operator request: run two real workflows, Dreaming and AI Hero support sweep.

Dreaming source repo: `/Users/joel/Code/joelhooks/pi-cloudflare-dream`.

Support source repo: `/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/aihero-support`.

Execution boundary:

- Dreaming is a system-scope memory/improvement workflow. It should explore JoelClaw network agent session transcripts across Pi, Codex, and Claude, hydrate transcript receipts, capture candidate memories and improvement proposals, and produce ShitRat/kernel update candidates.
- Dreaming may propose patches to Brain, prompts, skills, or kernel package surfaces, but the first pass should stop at reviewable artifacts unless each item has forward diff, rollback diff, pre-apply hash check, validation output, and apply receipt.
- AI Hero support sweep is a private support workflow in the AI Hero support cockpit. It should not leak customer/support memory into public workflow repo notes. It must preserve the AI Hero approval gate: no customer-visible Front reply, archive, assignment, tag, Kit write, Contact State write, sequence enrollment, refund, invoice, or sensitive account mutation without the repo's explicit approval rules and stale checks.
- If both workflows run in the same operator session, keep their artifacts separate: Dreaming writes ShitRat/session-memory candidates; AI Hero support writes private triage receipts, draft packs, and approval reports under the support repo.

Current execution gotcha: `joelclaw sessions search "pi-cloudflare-dream dreaming shitrat kernel session transcripts" --source both --machine dark-wizard --limit 5 --extract` failed because `dark-wizard.tail7af24.ts.net` could not resolve, and `joelclaw status` reported the server/worker unreachable. Direct Typesense access worked when `~/.config/system-bus.env` was loaded by the Dream repo. Standalone `joelclaw sessions search --source typesense` did not load that env path, and `joelclaw sessions signals --source typesense` reported that Typesense-only signal mining is unsupported because it needs role-aware raw transcript context.

